**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests`

**How to implement.** The Details bay credits the licensed entries of the selected element's binding: the bound entry and, for a sample, the materials of its layers (001 §B 'Licence attribution': in the Details view; the S3.3 brief: the Details view of a bound element). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, in the `type TableAndElementRotationModel with` block that holds `detailsState` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3187`): the public `member model.detailsAttributionLines : EntryAttributionLine list`. For `ElementSelected i` whose element has a bound entry (`boundEntry`, `:2449`), it is `model.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf entry.attributedEntryIds` (steps 101, 113, 114). It is `[]` on a read error, for an unbound element, and without an element selection. `detailsState` appends each line's `text` on its own line after the title and the out-of-band warning, so the Details bay (`BayNames.details`) shows the credit under what the element is. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) Tests, in `LayerBandsControlsTests`, over `initMain ()`, whose `catalogueImports` is the in-memory double its stores were imported through (step 101's `DefaultStores`). Step 113's `putSealedEntries` puts `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` (`CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`), `licensedMaterialContent` `RII glass` (`CC0-1.0`), and `sampleContentOver` `PTB stack` and `RII stack` over them; the double pushes each new entry into the model's stores. `the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation`: after `AddElement Sample` and the class's `bind` of the new element to `PTB stack`, `detailsAttributionLines` is exactly one line whose text is `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`. Bound to `RII stack`, it is `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0`, and bound to `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s sample, it is `[]`. `the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material`: the Details bay, mounted headless as `the Details bay renders the bound multilayer sample's bands and description` mounts it but without the `ui-smoke` trait, shows a `layerBandsTitle` whose text holds `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test` for an element bound to `PTB stack`.

**Acceptance.** After the Details bay is wired, `detailsAttributionLines` MUST credit a bound entry and the licensed materials of a bound sample, and the Details bay MUST show them; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation` and `the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.
